// RUN: runic-opt %s --verify-diagnostics

// A diagnostic of the frontend is checked against the expectations written in the input, like one
// of the IR path. The syntax error is expected on its line, and every diagnostic met and every
// expectation matched make a run that succeeds and prints nothing.

fn ok() = 1;
fn broken() = 1 +* 2; // expected-error {{expected an expression}}
